docs/reports/phase3.md:101:| 32 | `E` event log: newest first, kind/reason/bounded payload, masked env | DONE | Task 014 (this report's earlier rows used a different task-numbering scheme that called this Task 124; `tasks.json`'s id for the work is `014`). Store: `internal/store.Store.ListEvents(ctx, limit)` (`internal/store/store.go`) orders `ORDER BY at DESC, seq DESC` -- `seq` (an autoincrementing tiebreaker column already in the schema) makes the order deterministic even when two events share the same `at` timestamp, e.g. two actions inside one frozen-clock test tick -- and caps at `defaultEventLogLimit = 200` when no smaller limit is requested; covered by `internal/store/store_test.go`'s `TestListEventsOrdersNewestFirstAndCapsAtLimit`. TUI: `E` (global, gated only on the help overlay being closed, since the log spans every session rather than the presently selected one) opens `internal/tui/event_log.go`'s `eventLogView()`, listing every recorded event's relative time/kind/reason plus its payload, newest first; `updateEventLog` routes through the shared `applyDialogContract` with only `Cancel` set, so Esc closes it and it joins the mouse-guard/`View()`/key-dispatch gating lists like every other dialog (`m.eventLogOpen`, `grep -n 'm.eventLogOpen' internal/tui/tui.go` shows all three). With no store attached it renders "(event log is unavailable: no store is attached)" rather than panicking. Masking: `renderEventPayload()` calls `maskEventPayload()` first (JSON-decodes the payload; any object member whose key matches task 010's one `isSecretShapedKey` predicate has its value replaced the same way `maskEnvValue` does; a non-JSON payload passes through completely unchanged, since it cannot contain a key at all) and only then `truncateEventPayload()` (bounds at `maxEventLogPayloadRunes = 96` runes with an ellipsis via `m.glyph`) -- masking always happens before truncation, so a secret cannot be smuggled out by truncating the mask marker away. No real write path in this codebase puts a secret-shaped value into an event payload today (SPEC's "env values never enter events" rule holds -- `set_env`'s own recorded payload is the env key NAME only), so this is deliberately defensive/forward-looking, not a fix for a live leak; the masking is still exercised end-to-end against a real payload SHAPE rather than left as dead code. Go coverage: `internal/tui/event_log_test.go` (`TestEventLogViewOrdersEventsNewestFirstAndTruncatesALongPayload`, `TestEventLogViewMasksSecretShapedPayloadValueButNotOrdinaryOnes`, `TestEventLogOpensOnECapitalAndClosesOnEsc`, `TestEventLogViewWithNoStoreStatesUnavailableRatherThanPanicking`, `TestMaskEventPayloadLeavesNonJSONPayloadUnchanged`). Scenario: `features/event_log.feature` (`@requirement-32-event-log-newest-first`: three *real* product actions -- archiving a session, switching a claude session's permission profile, editing an env key -- produce three distinctly-kinded events, and the rendered order is asserted newest first via `FindText` row positions, which also differs from both insertion order and alphabetical order, ruling out an accidental match; `@requirement-32-event-log-masks-secret-shaped-payload`: a fixture row inserted directly into the `events` table, since no real write path produces a secret-shaped payload to exercise, carries a secret-shaped key's value beside an ordinary one, and task 011's own real-grid `screenGridNeverContains` scan -- never a substring search over the trimmed frame string -- confirms the secret value never reaches the screen while the ordinary value does). Help overlay documents `E`; guard-word lists in `cmd/deck/main_test.go`/`internal/tui/tui_test.go` updated. |
